@h1 Roadmap h1@

Where Wit is today and what comes next. Pre-1.0, breaking changes are allowed
under 0.x with notes.

@h2 Status now h2@

The language is feature-complete for its initial scope: nodes, definitions,
additive partials, records, collections, data access, conditionals, iteration,
and scripting all ship, along with two renderers (HTML and Markdown), a CLI, and
a VS Code extension.

@h2 The milestone ladder h2@

@ul
@li @strong M0–M4 strong@ — foundations, language lock, the lexer and parser, and
the resolver and expander. Shipped. li@
@li @strong M5 strong@ — the VS Code extension core: highlighting, diagnostics,
hover, go-to-definition, references, outline, and completion. Shipped. li@
@li @strong M6 strong@ — the reference renderer: HTML from any expanded AST.
Shipped. li@
@li @strong M7 (1.0) strong@ — the bar for 1.0 is a docs site, published packages,
and a versioned spec. This site is itself an M7 deliverable and a dogfood
test. li@
ul@

@h2 In progress — the literal-node layer h2@

A literal-content layer that builds toward a component system.

@ul
@li @strong Shipped. strong@ Literal nodes (@@@code @@name … name@@ code@@@) and
frozen bodies (@@@code @@@ … @@@ code@@@); @@@code {{path}} code@@@ interpolation
inside double-fence bodies, with single braces left literal so CSS works; and
style and script raw-text rendering in the default render path. li@
@li @strong Designed, not yet built. strong@ The component definition
(@@@code ##name … name## code@@@), a @code body code@ parameter, interpolation in
strings and normal content, capture scope with parameter defaults, and
component-CSS deduplication. li@
ul@

@h2 VS Code extension roadmap h2@

The extension core has shipped; the rest is committed future work, most of it
exposing engine capability that already exists to the editor.

@ul
@li @strong Quick wins. strong@ A live HTML preview panel, snippets for the
preferred forms, code folding, a file icon, and palette commands. li@
@li @strong Medium. strong@ Ctrl-clickable document links, rename-symbol, workspace
symbol search, signature help, and quick-fix code actions. li@
@li @strong Bigger bets. strong@ A formatter with format-on-save, embedded script
highlighting inside the script bridge, a custom split editor, and marketplace
publishing. li@
ul@

The value-per-effort priority is live preview, then snippets, then folding and
the file icon, then document links and rename.

@h2 Deferred to v2 h2@

Non-ASCII handles, incremental reparse hooks, and a separate theme package are
explicitly deferred. Two writer-delight candidates surfaced by onboarding are
worth naming honestly as @strong not yet shipped strong@: a build watch mode and
comma escaping inside record values.

@h2 What is not shipped h2@

@aside(class note) 💡 Do not treat these as available: the component definition
(@@@code ##name … name## code@@@), interpolation in ordinary prose, the
@@@code @name: … !! code@@@ form-fill invocation, a @code --watch code@ flag, and a
@code contains code@ conditional operator. They are planned, designed, or out of
scope — not present in the current release. aside@

